36-2. Set the redirect URL to `https://<your-app>/api/bank/callback`. Production apps accept only `https://` redirects, so `http://localhost` is rejected. To try the flow locally, register a second app in the **Sandbox** environment (it only reaches mock banks) with `http://localhost:3000/api/bank/callback`.
37-3. Let the control panel generate the key pair and keep the downloaded private key (`<application-id>.pem`), or upload your own public certificate and keep its private key.
38-4. In the control panel, link your own accounts to the application (activate it by linking accounts). Only linked accounts can be synced.
39-5. Set the environment variables in `.env`:
40-   - `ENABLE_BANKING_APP_ID`: the application ID
41-   - `ENABLE_BANKING_PRIVATE_KEY`: the PEM contents (one line with literal `\n` is fine)
42-   - `BANK_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY`: `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"`
43-   - `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` (the callback base) must also be set
44-6. Apply the new migrations, restart `npm run dev`, then use **Import → Connected banks → Choose a bank → Connect bank**.
45-
46-Consent usually lasts up to 180 days, depending on the bank. A reconnect banner appears 7 days before it ends. A daily cron (`/api/cron/bank-sync`, authorized by `CRON_SECRET`) syncs in the background. PSD2 allows about 4 background fetches a day per bank. **Sync now** runs with you present, so it doesn't count toward that limit. Pending transactions are not synced.
